  "advisory": {
    "temperament": "Cautiously Constructive. CPI MoM came in line (+0.1%) - the relief valve opened. But YoY re-accelerated sharply to 3.4% (from 2.5%), reminding the market that inflation isn't dead. Tech bouncing pre-market (+0.53% NQ) on the in-line print; energy sitting on yesterday's +4.6% XLE surge. VIX at 15.29 signals complacency - the market is not pricing tail risk. That's both good (no panic) and dangerous (no cushion).",
    "posture": "Lean in selectively on AI/energy, hold hedges, stay light overall. This is a single-idea-at-a-time day. Max 4 trades (MIXED regime). Lead with NQ OR Break if tech holds above PP at the open. CRWV gap-and-go is today's highest-conviction single-name. GLD is the portfolio hedge that works regardless of which way this resolves. Do NOT chase the broad market - let setups come to you.",
    "verdict": "\u26a1 LEAN IN with discipline. AI earnings (CRWV) confirm the secular theme. CPI in-line clears the near-term hurdle. But the rate hike clock is ticking (49% Sept probability) and oil at $87.86 is an embedded headwind. Use R1 breaks as entries, not FOMO. Size appropriately - this is a 4-trade day, not an 8-trade day."
